It explains that the state of an arhat is obtained by eleven faculties because that is possible for some arhats who restore frequent degeneration.[454] “Obtained by nine” is here explained from the perspective of simultaneous obtainment.
“Restoring degeneration” means that some arhats who obtain the state of an arhat dependent on any {of the six levels of} the feeling of equanimity on or above the fourth absorption {or unrestricted access concentration} restore the degenerated state in dependence on pleasure of the actual basis of the third absorption. If degeneration occurs {a second time,} it is restored in dependence on mental satisfaction of the first two absorptions. Therefore it is possible that the state of an arhat is obtained by eleven: (1–5) the five such as faith, (6) the mental faculty, (7) complete knowledge, (8) possessing complete knowledge, and (9–11) the three feelings. Though it degenerates many times, it is impossible that it is obtained by more faculties because it is impossible that restoration depends on faculties other than the three feelings. {It is also possible that it is obtained by ten if it degenerates once and is then restored.}
Question: It would also be possible that nonreturners heal the degenerated state through obtainment of eleven faculties because the method would be similar. [103]

