Vaibhāṣikas explain this to be valid scripture because a sūtra observes:
One becomes an ārya who abandons the five branches through generating the ten nonlearner Dharmas[546] and possessing each obtainment.[547]
“The five branches” refers to (1–2) two attachments to the two higher realms, (3) excitation, (4) pride, and (5) ignorance, which constitute the five factors associated with higher states. The term “ārya” here means an arhat. {Obtainment is substantially existent because its result is observed.}

