Master Pūrṇavardhana says:
The Autocommentary states: “It is well known that whoever generates it undoubtedly generates it again once it degenerates and is born among beings devoid of discernment.” The term “well known” indicates another [philosophical] system. And others say that it is either experienced after rebirth or its experience is uncertain.[559]
But whether or not it may have degenerated, when one sees the error in it through meeting a spiritual guide (kalyāṇamitra), one decides not to generate or manifest it. Further, persons {for whom such [false] liberation and its path manifest} are just ordinary beings. It is not manifested by āryas because through it beings are born as long-lived gods in abodes without leisure; āryas view that as a state of downfall {because āryas do not discern cyclic existence as liberation}. Therefore only childlike beings who discriminate it as liberation enter it. As such, meditation that stops all mental attention whatsoever is the meditative attainment of nondiscernment alone [147] because such meditation fulfills all such characteristics. Moreover, it is not obtained in the past or future but will be obtained in one instant, {which is the first moment of} the present alone, because {though mixed, it must be established through great exertion and} it is a mindless state. However, until relinquished, its past {obtainment} is possessed like pratimokṣa vows. {And since it is a mindless state, its future is not obtained.}

'gog pa'i snyoms par 'jug pa zhes gsungs pa'ang gong ma 'du shes med pa'i snyoms 'jug ji lta ba de bzhin du sems dang sems byung 'gog pa nyid do/ /
yid la byed pa la sogs pa la khyad par yod pas dang po yid la byed pa ni snyoms 'jug 'di ni 'du shes dang tshor ba zhi{ ba ni zhi ba'o snyam nas zhi} bar gnas pa'i don du snyoms par 'jug gi nges par 'byung bas ni ma yin no/ /
sa ni srid pa'i rtse mor skyes pa ste 'du shes med 'du shes med min skye mched la brten pa yin te/ phra ba phra ba'i mjug thogs su zhes 'byung bas sems phra ba'i mjug thogs su mtshungs ldan rnams dgag sla ba'i phyir dang*/{ de'i rnam smin la srid rtse'i phung po bzhi 'grub pas sam srid pa la rgyab kyis ltas shing sems mthar thug par spyod pa'i rnam thar de sa gzhan na med pas srid rtse'i sa pa'o/}

Objection: If those meditative attainments lack mind, in what way are they meditative attainments? For it is accepted that the mind engaged in absorption is in equipoise on its focal object.
Those schools respond that is not so because the great [155] elements are engaged to counterbalance the arising of mind through special mental attention, or because discernment and feeling are serially stopped by the power of the concentration generated in preparation for meditative attainment.
Yogācāras say that the nonarising of the six- or the sevenfold collection of consciousness on the basis of the foundation consciousness by the power of mental attention is called “meditative attainment.” {It is substantially existent because it can stop the arising of mind.}
{Vasubandhu asserts that it is not that minds do not arise because they were stopped by [the elements] but that, if minds did not arise because they were stopped by the mind of meditative attainment, then when minds do arise, an incompatible body or foundation consciousness would be generated. Moreover, the mere nonarising of future minds and mental factors would be designated as “meditative attainment.” And by designating the unarisen body or foundation consciousness as “meditative attainment,” such nonarising would then be asserted to be a conditioned state.}

{Objection: If the four characteristics are complete in one object at one time, it would follow that arising, disintegrating, enduring, and aging would occur at one time. If they were incomplete, it would not be a conditioned state.
Reply: Since arising functions for future objects that have not yet arisen and enduring and so on function for present objects, they exist at different times. Therefore there is no error.}
Objection: If conditioned states are generated by future arising, then all conditioned states would arise at once.

