Nominally there are seven, but there are six in terms of substance. There are two each respectively for the three paths of seeing, meditation, and no more learning: (1) followers of faith and (2) followers of reality, (3) those resolute in faith and (4) those obtaining results by insight, and (5) arhats liberated according to circumstances and (6) arhats liberated regardless of circumstances. {The others are not delineated by substance.}
Followers of faith are classified in three by intellectual faculty: those of sharp, medium, and dull intellectual faculty. There are five by type, such as those who degenerate and so on. There are fifteen by path, such as patience and knowledge. There are seventy-three by freedom from attachment since there are: (1) those who possess all the ties (bandhana) and do not abandon even one object to be abandoned by the path of meditation, and (2–73) those who are [progressively] free from attachment from the nine stages of affliction on the eight levels from the desire realm to nothingness. There are nine by basis: (1–3) the three human continents, because a human of Kuru is not a basis since the path does not exist there, and (4–9) the six desire-realm gods. Thus, if classified by faculty, type, path, freedom from attachment, and basis, there are 478,125. Also, beings of other types should be classified in this way.
Followers of reality, those obtaining results by insight, and arhats liberated regardless of circumstances [570] have no classification by type. But both those resolute in faith and arhats liberated according to circumstances are classified as five by type.

