And since one obtains all analytical knowledges if just one is obtained, none are obtained if any one is incomplete. {They all are the result of the same path.}
Some assert that the initial preparation, which is their cause, is obtained owing to being educated in astrology, the speech of the Buddha, grammar, and logic.
Vaibhāṣikas assert that preparation is obtained in all four solely through developing expertise in synonyms, essential natures, etymologies, and classifications found only in the speech of the Buddha. {This conforms with the Commentary on Rational System of Exposition, which states:
Synonyms act as the proximate cause of the analytical knowledge of phenomena. So too, defining characteristics [give rise to] the analytical knowledge of meaning, etymologies [give rise to] the analytical knowledge of language, and classifications [give rise to] the analytical knowledge of prowess.}[1823]
Their order is taught as follows: first, analytical knowledge of phenomena arises from comprehending the meaning after comprehending words and letters; then the knowledge of synonyms arises from the meaning; through that arising, knowledge of their etymology. Then, from those, the [629] unobstructed prowess of liberation arises. {Their order is first comprehending words and letters, then their meaning, then sentences containing one or two meanings and so on, and then the unobstructed knowledge of those meanings.}

yang mdo las/ mi slob pa'i rig pa ni gsum ste/ mi slob pa'i sngon gyi gnas rjes su dran pa shes pa mngon du byed pa'i rig pa dang*/ mi slob pa'i 'chi 'pho dang skye ba shes pa mngon du byed pa'i rig pa dang*/ mi slob pa'i zag pa zad pa shes pa mngon du byed pa'i rig pa'o zhes pa dang*/ sde snod gsum pa yin/ rig pa gsum pa yin zhes kyang gsungs pas gsum po de dag las kyang don dam par mi slob pa'ang yin la de'i rig pa'ang yin ni zag med yin pas tha ma zag zad kyi mngon shes kho na yin la/ dang po gnyis ni mi slob pa de'i rgyu la skyes pa'i phyir mi slob pa de'i rig pa zhes bya'i dngos su na de gnyis ni zag bcas yin pas slob gnyis ka ma yin pas mi slob pa ma yin no/ /
